Daśaratha sees sage-clad Rāma and loses consciousness --- Daśaratha laments past cruelty to creatures --- Daśaratha orders Sumantra to yoke chariot --- Daśaratha orders costly clothes and jewels for Sītā --- Sītā adorns herself and shines like sunlight --- Kausalyā bids Sītā honor exiled husband as god --- Sītā vows wifely dharma with lyre-chariot maxims --- Rāma consoles Kausalyā that fourteen years pass quickly --- Rāma begs forgiveness of three hundred fifty mothers --- Palace turns from drum-roar to lamentation
